# KHOR Beauty Clinic Full Stack Website

KHOR Beauty Clinic is a full stack web application built for a beauty clinic business. The project includes a public customer-facing website and an admin dashboard for managing bookings, enquiries, services, and payment statuses.

---

## Features

### Public Website

* Home page
* Services page
* About page
* Contact page
* Booking page
* Customer booking form
* Customer enquiry form
* WhatsApp contact link
* Responsive layout

### Admin Dashboard

* Admin login
* View bookings
* Add bookings
* Edit bookings
* Delete bookings
* Update booking status
* Update payment status
* View booking details
* Manage customer enquiries

---

## Tech Stack

### Frontend

* Next.js
* React
* TypeScript
* Tailwind CSS
* shadcn/ui
* Lucide React
* Sonner Toast Notifications

### Backend

* Node.js
* Express.js
* TypeScript
* Prisma ORM
* PostgreSQL
* JWT Authentication
* Helmet
* CORS
* Express Rate Limit

---

## Project Structure

```txt
project-root/
├── frontend/
│   ├── app/
│   ├── components/
│   ├── lib/
│   ├── public/
│   └── package.json
│
└── backend/
    ├── controllers/
    ├── middleware/
    ├── routes/
    ├── prisma/
    ├── services/
    ├── app.ts
    └── package.json
```

---

## Frontend Setup

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Default frontend URL:

```txt
http://localhost:3000
```

If port 3000 is occupied, Next.js may run on:

```txt
http://localhost:3001
```

---

## Backend Setup

```bash
cd backend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Default backend URL:

```txt
http://localhost:5000
```

---

## Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file inside the backend folder.

```env
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/database_name"
JWT_SECRET="your_jwt_secret"
PORT=5000
```

---

## Prisma Commands

Generate Prisma client:

```bash
npx prisma generate
```

Run database migration:

```bash
npx prisma migrate dev
```

Open Prisma Studio:

```bash
npx prisma studio
```

---

## Main API Endpoints

### Auth

```txt
POST /api/auth/login
```

### Bookings

```txt
POST   /api/bookings
GET    /api/bookings
PUT    /api/bookings/:id
DELETE /api/bookings/:id
```

### Enquiries

```txt
POST /api/enquiries
GET  /api/enquiries
```

### Services

```txt
GET /api/services
```

### Payments

```txt
GET /api/payments
```

---

## Authentication

The admin dashboard uses JWT authentication.

After login, the token is stored in localStorage and attached to protected API requests using the Authorization header.

```txt
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

---

## Security Features

* JWT authentication for admin routes
* Helmet for secure HTTP headers
* CORS configuration for frontend access
* Rate limiting to reduce spam requests
* Protected backend routes for admin actions

